WEBVTT

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:05.210
About 80% of the world's population

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:08.170
"Quirk"

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:08.670
is born with some kind of special trait,
a Quirk, in this superhuman society.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.670
I, Izuku Midoriya, was Quirkless,

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:17.850
but then I had a fateful meeting
with the number one hero, All Might,

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:22.060
and he transferred the Quirk,
One For All, to me.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.150
And then, I enrolled in the
hero course at U.A. High School,

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.110
the prestigious school that
has produced many heroes...

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:35.740
With my friends,
I continue to run toward my dream.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:40.790
This is the story of how
I became the greatest hero.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:00.760
<i>An ordinary moment dazzles</i>

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.310
<i>Enough to make you close your eyes</i>

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:07.980
<i>A ray of light is thrown</i>

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:11.610
<i>Into the dark unnoticed</i>

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:15.070
<i>Lost and confused in dreams</i>

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:18.530
<i>A tiny star falls down your cheeks</i>

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:22.290
<i>I give you a beat of my sound</i>

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:25.620
<i>Wiping away your fears</i>

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:31.880
<i>Put the new colors onto your past</i>

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:36.170
<i>Rainbow for the future</i>
<i>Hold up the palette</i>

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:38.890
<i>Show me your colors</i>

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:43.470
<i>The only thing I always hope</i>

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:46.640
<i>Through all the lousy nights</i>

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:48.520
<i>Right or wrong</i>
<i>Wrong or right</i>

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:50.440
<i>It doesn't matter to me</i>

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:54.320
<i>Just want to see you smile</i>

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:57.860
<i>Once in a lifetime</i>
<i>The sparkle of a moment</i>

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:00.950
<i>No, that prayer is too small</i>

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:04.490
<i>Make our belief intense</i>
<i>Jump over the fence</i>

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:08.040
<i>You can go anywhere</i>

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:12.750
<i>Cause we're the heroes</i>

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:22.010
"Make It! Do-or-Die Survival Training, Part 1"

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:27.770
To prepare for the upcoming
provisional hero licensing exam,

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:33.980
the first years of U.A.'s hero course
continued their intensive training.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.650
Most years, the provisional licensing exam

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:41.990
includes a section on disaster rescue.

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:43.280
So, today...

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:50.830
A TEAM: 
Tsuyu Asui
Tenya Iida
Ochaco Uraraka
Denki Kaminari
Eijiro Kirishima
 Fumikage Tokoyami
Shoto Todoroki
 Katsuki Bakugo
Izuku Midoriya
Momo Yaoyorozu

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:50.830
B TEAM: 
Yuga Aoyama
 Mina Ashido
 Mashirao Ojiro
Koji Koda
 Rikido Sato
 Mezo Shoji
 Kyoka Jiro
Hanta Sero
 Toru Hagakure
 Minoru Mineta

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:47.040
...we will split the class into two teams of ten

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.170
and have a training based on something
similar to what will be on the exam.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:53.170
"Tenya Iida"

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:53.500
I'm on Team A?

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:57.050
"Ochaco Uraraka"

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.300
Iida, Tsu, we're on the same team, huh?

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.210
Let's do our best.

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:58.920
"Ochaco Uraraka"                   "Tsuyu Asui"

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.970
Yeah, ribbit, ribbit.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.930
"Denki Kaminari"    "Eijiro Kirishima"

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:00.590
Let's do this.

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:02.430
Leave it to me!

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:08.640
"Momo Yaoyorozu"

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:05.220
Teamwork is important in rescue training.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:09.060
I look forward to working
with you, Todoroki, Tokoyami.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:11.140
"Momo Yaoyorozu"
"Shoto Todoroki"    "Fumikage Tokoyami"

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:09.730
Yeah.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:11.900
Let's give it our all.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:15.940
"Katsuki Bakugo"    "Izuku Midoriya"

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:15.690
I'm on the same team as that damn Deku, huh?

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:18.740
Rescue training, huh?

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:21.360
I wonder what we'll be doing...

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:25.280
Now, we will begin the rescue training.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:30.460
"Ground Beta"

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.500
Everyone change into your costumes
immediately and go to Ground Beta.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:37.590
I, class representative Tenya Iida, have
been designated as the leader of Team A.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:43.430
Everyone, let us complete this rescue training
so we do not bring shame to U.A.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:47.350
In order to do that, your drive and
hard work will be necessary, but regarding...

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:50.980
He's still talking...
He always talks for so long...

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:53.310
Come on, let's just start the training already!

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:56.310
Everyone, I understand your eagerness,

00:03:56.310 --> 00:04:00.690
but let us consider the situation
one more time before we begin.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:03.740
Yes, it's just as Yaoyorozu says.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:06.240
Two hours ago,

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:10.500
a fire broke out on the bottom floor
of a large underground shopping mall.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.370
Currently, the fire has been put out,

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:15.380
and the people inside have been evacuated.

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:18.040
However, we received word that
somewhere in this underground mall,

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:21.880
there is still one person
who needs to be rescued.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:26.720
Our mission is to rescue
that person as quickly as possible.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:29.510
The person who needs
to be rescued is a training dummy.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:32.600
The power is out underground due to the fire,

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:35.810
but luckily, the emergency
power is still working.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:38.860
Then we should be able
to search even without light.

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:41.990
Searching for the person in
there will be a race against time.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:43.990
I propose we split up for the search.

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:48.120
Wait a minute. I'm not getting a signal here.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:48.990
You're right.

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:50.910
I'm not getting a signal, either.

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:56.000
So the fire probably made the relay
base station go down in this scenario.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.290
If that's the case,

00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:01.170
then even if we split up to search,
we should decide where to meet up after.

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:04.050
This mall goes down six floors.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:08.510
What if we go down from the central
stairwell and search floor B1 first,

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:11.350
then meet back up at the
central stairwell ten minutes later

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:15.730
to move down another
floor together and search there?

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:17.650
I agree with Tsu!

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.360
I do, too.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.570
Wait, Kacchan! Where are you going?

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.490
Isn't it obvious?

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:26.700
I'm going to look for the damn citizen
who didn't escape in time.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.530
Wait a minute, Bakugo!

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:31.240
Don't go off on your own
and interfere with our teamwork.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:33.120
We should do as Asui suggests and--

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.660
Call me "Tsu."

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:37.830
We should do as <i>T-Tsu</i> suggests and--

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:41.920
You guys are the ones saying
the search is a race against time.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:47.720
I'll find that damn citizen in no time
and show you the difference between us.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:48.720
Kacchan!

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.010
Wait up, Bakugo.

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:51.260
It's dangerous to go by yourself.

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:52.560
I'll go with you.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:54.270
Then, I guess I'll go, too.

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:56.690
Kirishima and Kaminari, you guys, too?

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:59.940
We'll meet you by the
central stairwell in ten minutes!

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:02.860
We'll try to bring Bakugo with us, too!

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:06.070
R-Right, okay. Be careful.

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:08.410
Bakugo's the same as ever, huh?

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:10.120
Self-centered.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:13.450
A-Anyway, we shouldn't
keep standing around here.

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:16.370
Let's split up and start searching, too.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.920
Thinking about the Quirks needed for rescue,

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:21.880
how about Midoriya, Uraraka, and Asui...

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:24.130
...Todoroki and Tokoyami...

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:28.680
...and Iida and I, splitting into three groups?

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:33.600
I see. Yaoyorozu split us up
into really well-balanced groups.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:37.310
In my group, there's Asui,
who's good in any terrain,

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:39.850
Uraraka, with her Zero Gravity,

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:42.400
and me, with my power fighting style.

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:43.940
With the three of us,

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:49.530
even if the person who needs rescuing is
stuck under debris, we could get them out.

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:55.040
On the other hand, in Iida's group
is Yaoyorozu, whose Quirk is Creation.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:07:00.540
With those two, they could deal
with any situation that comes up.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:04.670
And Todoroki and Tokoyami's group...

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:08.170
Dark Shadow's search ability
and power are great for this,

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:13.090
and Todoroki's Half-Cold, Half-Hot
should be able to do a lot in a disaster area.

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:18.100
And Dark Shadow's weak point,
that it's hard to control in the dark,

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:20.730
could be covered by the flames, too.

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:24.230
They're really well-thought-out.

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:26.440
The only problem I can see is,

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:30.700
if the emergency lights go out
and everything goes dark,

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:33.070
--our group is the only one
without the ability to produce light, but...

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:34.740
--Deku, Deku.
--our group is the only one
without the ability to produce light, but...

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:36.740
Deku!

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:38.120
Oh, where's everyone else?

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.290
--They already left.
--Huh?

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:43.380
Let's start searching, too, Midoriya.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:47.630
R-Right. We need to hurry up and
save that person who needs rescuing!

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:52.760
It's pretty spacious.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:53.720
Yeah.

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:55.970
But it's brighter than expected.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:58.220
We shouldn't have any problems
searching like this.

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:00.390
Deku, where should we start looking?

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:03.270
The fire happened on the bottom floor,

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:05.150
so the person we need to rescue

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:09.730
probably tried to head up to
the surface after noticing the fire.

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:11.400
But if they still didn't make it out,

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:13.820
then there's a possibility that
they're stuck behind some fire shutters.

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:16.660
They might be around the stairs somewhere here.

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:17.700
Let's go see.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.700
Ribbit.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:23.670
Looks like they're not on this floor.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:27.500
Let's look carefully until our time is up.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:30.340
Tokoyami, is this level of brightness okay?

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:33.170
I am having no difficulty
controlling Dark Shadow.

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:36.800
Bakugo, stop going off on your own.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.390
I never told you to follow me!

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:45.560
Shutters are closed all over the place.

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:47.730
It's like a maze.

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.520
The stairs are...

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:50.360
Ribbit?!

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:51.780
What's that?!

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.110
This is...?!

00:08:53.110 --> 00:08:54.450
An earthquake?

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:56.200
It's shaking, it's shaking!

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:58.280
Let go of me, damn it!

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:00.790
The floor!

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:02.910
The light's gone, too!

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:04.120
R-Ribbit!

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:05.620
--Asui!
--Tsu!

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:09.040
One For All, Full Cowling...

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:12.050
...Shoot Style!

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:16.470
Oh, no--

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:18.050
Deku!

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:37.410
Deku! Deku!

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:44.410
Wh-Where are we...?

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:46.960
Are you okay? You're not hurt?

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:49.380
I-I'm fine...

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:53.000
Thanks, you saved me.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:54.800
It was nothing.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:57.300
Oh, I'll release you now, okay?

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:07.520
I-I wonder how far we dropped...

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:11.400
I don't know... Anyway,
let's figure out where we are first.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:13.820
Wait, where's Asui?

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:15.610
Call me "Tsu."

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:18.400
Ribbit?

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:20.240
Tsu, you're okay!

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.320
I'm so glad!

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:24.540
But it looks like our situation isn't very good.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:28.830
All the exits and entrances
to this floor are blocked by debris.

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:31.420
And look at the ceiling...

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:34.460
I see. We need to find a way out.

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:39.180
Then, why don't you just use your
super strength to blow away the debris?

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:41.430
He can't do that, Ochaco.

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:43.100
Huh? Why not?

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:45.770
Listen carefully.

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:52.150
This sound...

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:54.110
The debris is falling...

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:57.360
The underground mall hasn't settled yet.

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:02.950
Yes. If you remove debris forcibly,
then you might cause it to collapse more.

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:04.030
In that case,

00:11:04.030 --> 00:11:07.450
we have no choice but to move each piece
of debris out of the way, one-by-one.

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:10.040
If we use your Zero Gravity--

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:12.170
Right. Leave it to me.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.260
Is anyone there?

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:19.130
Deku, that voice just now...

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:21.130
It's Yaoyorozu.

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:26.310
Hello? Is anyone there? Iida has been injured!

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:28.180
Iida's injured?

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:30.020
It sounds like it's coming from there.

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:32.190
Yaoyorozu, this is Midoriya!

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:35.440
Uraraka and Asu--I mean, Tsu, are with me, too!

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:37.780
We're heading your way now!

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:40.490
Midoriya! Thank you!

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:45.120
Please make some glue
to keep the debris from falling!

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:46.870
All right!

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:52.080
It's been about ten minutes since the shaking.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:55.710
Since there haven't been any aftershocks,
we can probably assume this isn't an earthquake

00:11:55.710 --> 00:11:59.920
but that part of the
underground mall is collapsing.

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:03.220
Todoroki, I'm grateful.

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:06.600
If you hadn't created
a sheet of ice over my head,

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:09.100
then I would be buried under debris right now.

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:12.270
It's only natural to save your friends, right?

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:15.480
But it'll be hard without any light.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:19.980
Yeah, it'll be hard to control
Dark Shadow in this darkness.

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:22.200
If Dark Shadow goes out of control...

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:25.240
...then there will be even more collapsing.

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:29.990
I could let Dark Shadow out
if you continuously made flames, though.

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:31.660
Let's not do that.

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:34.000
If I make flames in a place buried by debris,

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:35.460
then it could use up all our oxygen,

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:38.750
and we could get carbon monoxide poisoning.

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:43.220
I won't use my flames unless
it's absolutely necessary.

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:47.550
We cannot resume training like this.

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:51.850
If we wait here,
I'm sure the teachers will come get us.

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:55.520
You're right. That's probably true.

00:12:55.520 --> 00:13:00.980
But there's also the possibility that
this collapse was part of the training.

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:03.900
Escape from a secondary disaster, huh?

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:06.780
Either way, I'm worried about our classmates.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:11.410
Someone might've been
injured in the collapse earlier.

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:13.830
We need to make sure everyone's okay.

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:18.080
You're right. I completely agree
with everything you said.

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:26.090
Man, that was terrible!

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:28.930
Hey, you still alive, Kaminari?

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:31.260
S-Somehow...

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:35.940
But man, Bakugo was amazing, as usual.

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:40.860
If he hadn't blasted the debris coming down
from the ceiling into little pieces,

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:43.150
we would've been hurt bad.

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:45.110
What're you saying?

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:47.070
You're the one who protected me

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:50.660
from the pieces that flew out of
the explosion with your Hardening.

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:53.790
I mean, I'm the only one
who hasn't done anything.

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:54.910
I'm just excess baggage.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:56.750
That's not true.

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:59.080
What, are you stupid?

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:00.590
Bakugo!

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:03.300
Hey, you don't have to say it to my face.

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:05.130
I already know that!

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:06.920
No, stupid!

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:08.550
You said it again!

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:13.810
Listen! Your Quirk is the one
we need most for getting out of here!

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:16.850
You don't even know that, Dunce Face?

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:18.520
Bakugo...

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:21.190
Just save your Quirk.

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:23.070
Hey, what should we do now?

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:26.490
What should we do? Get out of here, duh.

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:28.860
We can't be looking around
for someone to rescue right now.

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:31.740
I mean, <i>we're</i> the ones
who need rescuing right now.

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:34.950
The teachers know what's
going on down here, right?

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:38.080
So, if we wait here, won't they come save us...?

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:42.540
Yeah, if we move without thinking,
we might make more things collapse...

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:44.210
Hey, where are you going?!

00:14:44.210 --> 00:14:45.510
Isn't it obvious?

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:48.380
I'm going to look for the damn citizen
who didn't escape in time.

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:51.550
Hey, wait up! This is just training.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:54.310
The person who needs rescuing's
just a training dummy!

00:14:54.310 --> 00:14:56.100
With everything else going on, we don't need--

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:57.980
All Might would go.

00:14:57.980 --> 00:14:59.600
Huh?

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:05.320
I'm saying that whether it's training
or whatever, All Might would go save them.

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:09.860
If the number one hero can do it,
then I better be able to do it, too.

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:14.280
I'll clear this damn
little training in a second.

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:17.370
Hey, wait! You're getting too worked up!

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:19.290
Bakugo, I'll go with you!

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:20.330
Kirishima?

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:21.620
I mean, he's right.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:25.710
Once we get our provisional licenses,
we can do real hero work.

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:29.590
When that happens, we might be
in a situation like this one day.

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:33.050
Would a hero leave someone
who needs rescuing and run away?

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:34.890
No, he wouldn't!

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:38.310
Crimson Riot would never do that!

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:40.060
That's why I won't run!

00:15:40.060 --> 00:15:43.230
Kirishima, you're getting too worked up, too!

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:46.270
Don't get in my way, Weird Hair!

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:49.240
I won't! Let's go!

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:52.910
Hey, hey, hey, hey... You're really going?

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:54.660
Wait for me! I'll go too!

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:57.790
I don't want to be left alone!

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.260
Everyone!

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:14.930
Iida...

00:16:14.930 --> 00:16:16.760
During the collapse...

00:16:18.430 --> 00:16:19.970
Yaoyorozu!

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:30.190
Iida protected me and injured his leg...

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:32.360
He hit his head hard, too...

00:16:33.110 --> 00:16:36.320
But his condition seems stable.

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:40.450
I also administered first aid
to the injury on his leg.

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:41.910
Iida!

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:44.290
Iida, hang in there.

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:48.420
W-We have to hurry up and save...

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:50.920
Iida...

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:54.130
He's still thinking about the rescue
even in his delirious state...

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:57.430
Let's get Iida somewhere safe, quickly.

00:16:57.430 --> 00:16:59.470
But how...?

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:02.270
It would take hours to move
each piece of debris individually

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:05.480
to get to the surface...

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:09.070
Let's go to the elevator lobby.

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:15.610
If the elevators didn't collapse,

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:19.370
then with Uraraka's Quirk,
we can get to the first floor in one go.

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:23.660
Everyone, this isn't training.

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:25.330
It's a real rescue.

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:27.500
Let's save Iida no matter what!

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:29.250
--Yeah!
--Ribbit!
--Yes!

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:31.880
We'll definitely save him.

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:33.300
Definitely!

00:17:43.890 --> 00:17:47.940
This is floor B6,
the bottom floor of the mall, huh?

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:50.400
Aw man, it's a mess.

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:53.690
How are we supposed to find someone in this?

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:56.700
Kirishima, where's the place
with the least damage?

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:58.240
What're you asking out of the blue for...?

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:00.870
Probably that place furthest back over there?

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:03.200
That's the only place
where the walls haven't collapsed.

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:04.950
All right, let's go!

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:06.160
Go...?

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:07.500
Where?

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:14.510
Idiot, the sturdiest place is where
the emergency power is, of course!

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:19.970
I knew it.

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:22.600
Everything's broken from the debris.

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:25.060
Hey, idiot! It's your turn.

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:28.270
Huh? For what?

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:32.110
Forget that! Just send your damn
electricity into these spare batteries!

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:34.110
R-Right...

00:18:34.110 --> 00:18:36.490
I see! Bakugo wants to fix the emergency power

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:40.570
to make it easier for everyone else to escape.

00:18:40.570 --> 00:18:43.780
Stop dragging your feet, damn it! I'll kill you.

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:46.540
Okay, okay.

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:48.250
If that's the case,

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:52.250
then I'll give it my all to make up
for not doing anything before!

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:55.250
Take this! All-Out Shock 2 Million Vo--

00:18:55.250 --> 00:18:59.180
The batteries'll break if you put in that much!

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:02.300
Okay, okay, I'll do it properly.

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:04.010
Charge, charge...

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:05.680
Rapid charging!

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:13.150
Ochaco.

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:14.900
Release.

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:20.610
We should be at the elevators soon.

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:21.780
Uraraka, are you all right?

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:23.070
Are you feeling sick?

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:27.870
I-I'm fine. We need to save Iida.

00:19:27.870 --> 00:19:29.620
If I get tired after just this,

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:32.000
then I won't be able to pass
the provisional licensing exam.

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:35.590
Ochaco, just a little more. You can do it!

00:19:35.590 --> 00:19:39.590
I know. Plus Ultra... right?

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:45.640
Just a little more... Just a little more...

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:53.230
If only Uraraka or Yaoyorozu were here.

00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:55.400
If only we had some light...

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:57.940
We can't do anything about what we don't have.

00:19:57.940 --> 00:19:58.940
Let's do this.

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:02.530
Oh, no!

00:20:03.610 --> 00:20:05.160
Todoroki!

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:12.750
Calm down, Dark Shadow!

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:19.550
What's this shaking?!

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:22.340
Deku!

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:23.550
It's now or never!

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:25.800
One For All... Full Cowling!

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:30.850
Todoroki!

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:32.640
Quiet down, Dark Shadow!

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:36.520
Please, calm down!

00:20:48.490 --> 00:20:49.910
Th-There's light...

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:52.460
All right! Emergency power's back!

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:54.670
Now, we just have to find that damn citizen!

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:57.750
Yeah! But that shaking earlier...

00:20:57.750 --> 00:20:58.880
There's no time!

00:20:58.880 --> 00:20:59.750
Hurry up!

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:01.210
Right!

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:04.340
W-Wait for--yay...

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:07.390
Todoroki! Hang in there, Todoroki!

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:10.100
Sorry...

00:21:10.100 --> 00:21:12.100
I think I blacked out for a second...

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:15.980
I'm sorry, too, about Dark Shadow.

00:21:15.980 --> 00:21:18.860
You don't need to apologize.

00:21:18.860 --> 00:21:21.070
All's well that ends well.

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:25.570
But it wasn't over yet.

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:34.290
This rescue training based
on the provisional licensing exam--

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:38.170
No, this survival training's real test...

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:39.670
...was about to begin.

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:43.670
Yes, about to begin...
